# A character is engulfed, dies, and answers the death prompt "n": does the
# prompt leave the screen? (bd inc-djbtl) Read the result with
# tools/check_stale_death_prompt.sh.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/low-dex-orc-barbarian-seed18-gate.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/engulf-stale-prompt.keys <seed>
#
# THE DEFECT. While the player is engulfed, the map pane shows the engulfer's
# inside instead of the dungeon. TextTerm::ShowMap's engulfed branch never
# cleared UpdateMap, and TextTerm::yn cleared the wrong window, so an answered
# yes/no prompt stayed on screen. (src/Term.cpp)
#
# THE STAGING. A frozen character (Hurk, an orc barbarian with DEX 7, Reflex -1;
# tools/fixtures/chars/low-dex-orc-barbarian-seed18-gate.sheet.txt) is loaded, so
# no chargen or lib change can alter him. His low Dex is why the Reflex save
# fails often. Wizard mode (w, y) offers
# "Monster Summoning" (src/Debug.cpp case 6); the stunjelly lands one square
# east, RIGHT ENTER picks that square. The jelly engulfs on a hit followed by a
# failed Reflex save (DC 15). The settings file tools/gates/Options.Dat sets
# OPT_ELUDE_DEATH to 3, which makes the game ask "Die? [yn]" at death instead of
# ending the game.
#
# WHY THE LOOPS ARE ON SCREEN TEXT. Whether and when the jelly hits, the save
# fails, and the character dies are rolls no control fixes (the catalog in
# docs/VERIFICATION.md has none for monster AI or a save for one creature).
# So each wait is "@until <text> ." : pass a turn (.) until the text appears.
# @until is bounded by SK_LOOP_MAX (src/Wposix.cpp), and a bound hit ends the
# session with "the key script looked for something", which the check reports
# as could-not-measure, never as pass or fail.
#
# THE DUMPS, in order: summoned (jelly in view, before the wait), engulfed
# (the word "Engulfed" is on screen), prompt (the live "Die? [yn]"), answered
# (after "n"; the defect is "Die? [yn]" still on this one).

@dump:arrival

# Wizard mode: summon a stunjelly one square east.
w
y
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "stunjelly"
RIGHT
ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:summoned

# Wait, a turn at a time, until the jelly engulfs.
@until "Engulfed" .
@dump:engulfed

# Wait until the character dies and the game asks.
@until "Die? [yn]" .
@dump:prompt

# Decline to die. The prompt must leave the screen.
n
@dump:answered
@quit
